    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_title">Privacy Policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_headline">Your screenshots stay on your device.</string>
    <string name="privacy_body">ML Kit reads text and sorts screenshots on your phone. Trove sends no screenshots, thumbnails, or extracted text anywhere. Usage data stays off unless you turn it on in Settings.</string>
    <string name="privacy_updated">Last updated September 19, 2026</string>
    <string name="privacy_intro">This policy explains what Trove accesses, what it keeps, and what you control. Trove is built to work entirely on your phone.</string>
    <string name="privacy_accesses_title">What Trove accesses</string>
    <string name="privacy_accesses_body">Trove reads the screenshots in your photo library so it can organize and search them. It asks for read-only photo access. On Android 14 and later you can grant access to selected photos instead of your whole library. Trove reads the image files and their details, such as date, size, and the app that took them.</string>
    <string name="privacy_stores_title">What Trove stores</string>
    <string name="privacy_stores_body">Trove keeps a private database on your phone. It holds the text recognized in your screenshots, their categories, and anything you add yourself: tags, notes, favorites, and collections. It also keeps your settings and a cache of thumbnails. Your screenshot files are never copied or moved. This data is excluded from Android backups.</string>
    <string name="privacy_processing_title">How screenshots are read</string>
    <string name="privacy_processing_body">Text recognition uses Google ML Kit running on your phone. The recognition model ships inside Trove, so screenshots are not sent to Google or anyone else to be read.</string>
    <string name="privacy_sharing_title">What leaves your phone</string>
    <string name="privacy_sharing_body">Nothing, unless you choose to send it. Trove has no account, no ads, and no internet permission. It does not upload screenshots, thumbnails, recognized text, or your library. When you use Share, the screenshot goes to the app you pick, and Trove has no say in what that app does with it.</string>
    <string name="privacy_usage_title">Usage data</string>
    <string name="privacy_usage_body">Share anonymous usage data is off by default. Trove currently has no internet permission, so it cannot send usage data even if you turn the switch on. If that changes, this policy will be updated first.</string>
    <string name="privacy_permissions_title">Permissions Trove asks for</string>
    <string name="privacy_permissions_body">Photos: to find and display your screenshots. Notifications and a foreground service: to show progress while Trove reads your screenshots in the background. Trove does not ask for your location, contacts, microphone, camera, or files outside your photo library.</string>
    <string name="privacy_control_title">Your choices</string>
    <string name="privacy_control_body">You can turn off background scanning, clear the image cache, and re-read your screenshots at any time from Settings. Secure screen hides Trove in recent apps and blocks screenshots of it. Trove only deletes a screenshot after you confirm. Revoke photo access in Android settings and Trove can no longer read your library. Uninstalling Trove removes all of its data.</string>
    <string name="privacy_changes_title">Changes to this policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_changes_body">If this policy changes, the new version appears here with an updated date.</string>
    <string name="privacy_contact_title">Contact</string>
    <string name="privacy_contact_body">Questions about this policy or your data? Email stormz5m@proton.me.</string>
